Univers42/Inception: make srcs/requirements/nginx/Dockerfile parseable again.

Docker's parser ends a line continuation at the backslash. Anything after it
on the same line is not a comment, it is the end of the instruction -- so the
inline `# ...` notes on the RUN block's continuation lines cut the instruction
in two and `: "bust=${CACHE_BUST}"` becomes an instruction of its own:

    ERROR: dockerfile parse error on line 16: unknown instruction: :

Two editor artifacts ride along on the same block: a stray `+` after
`apk update -q \` and a literal `<F6>` after `apk add nginx \`.

Measured 2026-09-12 against upstream main (2e2962b) and 9e74aaa, both from a
pristine `git clone` inside the b2r guest: nginx is the first image compose
builds, so the whole stack dies here and `make inception` never reaches the
other seven images. With this patch applied: 8 images, 534.1 MB, all eight
containers healthy, https 200 inside the guest and from the host.

The comments are kept -- moved above the RUN, where the parser is happy to
have them.

This lives in born2root because born2root is what pushes Inception into the
VM; the real home for it is a commit in Univers42/Inception.
Apply with:  git -C <inception> apply /path/to/this/file

diff --git a/srcs/requirements/nginx/Dockerfile b/srcs/requirements/nginx/Dockerfile
index 4b8b8e2..fee9270 100644
--- a/srcs/requirements/nginx/Dockerfile
+++ b/srcs/requirements/nginx/Dockerfile
@@ -12,19 +12,27 @@ ARG APK_CACHE_ID=apk
 #  CACHE_BUST=$(date +%s)) and Docker sees a different instruction string, so it invalidtates the cache
 #  and actually re-runs apk update/apk add, pulling resh package version of resuing an old cache layer.
 ARG CACHE_BUST=0
-RUN --mount=type=cache,id=${APK_CACHE_ID}-nginx,sharing=locked,target=/var/cache/apk \ # a buildkit cache mount
+# --mount=type=cache is a BuildKit cache mount. It can only attach to one
+# exact path (target=/var/cache/apk):
+# https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#run---mounttypecache
+# apk caches packages at /etc/apk/cache by default, so that path is symlinked
+# onto the mount for the duration of the step and the symlink is removed
+# afterwards, so no dangling symlink is left in the image.
+# Alpine's default nginx config ships its own ssl_protocols line (often with
+# older TLS versions). The sed rewrites it in place to force TLS 1.2/1.3 only,
+# satisfying the subject's TLS requirement without hand-writing nginx.conf.
+# /run/nginx holds nginx's runtime PID/socket files; /etc/nginx/ssl is where
+# the entrypoint script copies the cert and key.
+RUN --mount=type=cache,id=${APK_CACHE_ID}-nginx,sharing=locked,target=/var/cache/apk \
     : "bust=${CACHE_BUST}" \
-    # buildKit cache mount can only attack to one exact path - target=/var/cache/apk
-    # https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#run---mounttypecache
-    && ln -sf /var/cache/apk /etc/apk/cache \   # alpine apk tool by default caches packages at /etc/apk/cache
-    && apk update -q \  +
-    && apk add nginx \<F6>
-    # alpine's default nginx cofig ships with its own ssl_protocols line (often includes older TLS version or default) this rewrites it in-place ot force only TLS 1.2/1.3 satisfying the subject TLS requirement without hand-writing the whole nginx.conf
+    && ln -sf /var/cache/apk /etc/apk/cache \
+    && apk update -q \
+    && apk add nginx \
     && sed -i 's/^\([[:space:]]*\)ssl_protocols .*/\1ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;/' /etc/nginx/nginx.conf \
-    && rm /etc/apk/cache \ # remove the symlink which avoid having a dangling/pointless symlink 
+    && rm /etc/apk/cache \
     && mkdir -p \
-        /run/nginx \    # for its runtime PID/SOCKET files, and 
-        /etc/nginx/ssl  # the destination of the entrypoint scirpt copies the cert/key
+        /run/nginx \
+        /etc/nginx/ssl
 
 # configuration repo's config
 COPY conf/nginx.conf /etc/nginx/http.d/default.conf.template
